# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is content-addressed in several places: test fixtures and fuzz corpus seeds are
# hashed byte-for-byte (SHA-256) and compared against committed digests. A Windows checkout that
# rewrites LF to CRLF changes those bytes and breaks the digest comparison, so line endings are
# pinned to LF everywhere rather than left to the platform default.

# Normalise text files to LF in the repository and in every working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact assets: never translate these, in either direction. Their bytes ARE the contract.
#
#   crates/pid-core/tests/fixtures/**   csxpid_reference.json is hashed in tests/common/mod.rs
#                                       and checked against csxpid_reference.json.sha256
#   crates/pid-runlog/tests/fixtures/** golden run-log schema fixtures (v1/v2 migration)
#   fuzz/corpus/**                      seeds covered by fuzz/corpus/SHA256SUMS
crates/pid-core/tests/fixtures/** -text
crates/pid-runlog/tests/fixtures/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text

# Preserve the submitted external audit Markdown byte-for-byte, including its authored hard-break
# spaces, without treating those spaces as repository-authored whitespace errors.
audit/evidence/external-model-pid-rs-deep-audit-2026-08-12.md -whitespace

# Preserve the official LPPL 1.3c license copy byte-for-byte. Its upstream trailing spaces are
# part of the reviewed source bytes, not repository-authored whitespace errors.
LICENSE-LPPL-1.3c -text -whitespace

# Preserve the three installed font-license/package-manifest observations byte-for-byte. The
# retained Source Sans and Latin Modern source files include upstream whitespace that is part of
# their digest-bound evidence, not repository-authored formatting.
audit/formal/latex/mathematical-results-guide/font-licenses/gust-font-license-1.0-tex-live-2024.txt -text -whitespace
audit/formal/latex/mathematical-results-guide/font-licenses/manifest-latin-modern-2.004-tex-live-2024.txt -text -whitespace
audit/formal/latex/mathematical-results-guide/font-licenses/source-sans-pro-ofl-1.1-tex-live-2024.txt -text -whitespace

# Rejected-route archive payloads are content-addressed historical bytes. Do not normalize their
# line endings or treat retained source whitespace as current repository-authored formatting.
audit/archive/ksg-m1a-rejected-lifecycle-checker-20260828/payload/** -text -whitespace
audit/archive/numerical-claim-history-20260725/payload/** -text -whitespace
audit/archive/sxpid3-s1-historical-checkers-v1/payload/** -text -whitespace
